  "id": "between-subjects-factor",
  "term": "between-subjects factor",
  "definition": "A between-subjects factor is a variable in a study that separates participants into different groups, with each person belonging to only one group. In the example provided, skill level is a between-subjects factor because participants are classified as either experts or novices.",
